Z||000000||pherder||08-02-2001||03:05 PM||||What would you think would be better?<P>Not so fast there!  I have some interesting information.<P>Seems I needed to replace the struts on my wife's Mazda Protege DX and the wheels (stock steel wheels were ALL out of round!  You would think they would last longer than 10 years and 140,000 miles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P>Ordered all from The Tire Rack and had them shipped and delivered in two days!!!<P>The only struts they offered were KYB but at a reasonable price (~$51 each)  I installed them only to find that one was defective (one squeaked really bad and got <B>VERY</B> hot after driving it ~ 15 miles).  Due to needing the wife's car up and running ASAP, I purchased a Gabriel gas strut from a local Auto Zone (~$41) to replace the squeaking KYB.  Upon disassembly, I found that they were the <B>EXACT</B> same strut!  The part number, and all the stamped writing on the strut was the same!  The only difference was the "KYB" decal on the strut (which was falling off after only one day on the car!)  The included paperwork on how to install the strut (generic instructions) and the "bump" stop plastic was the same also.<P>Looks like one place built the strut and it is sold to all the different strut companies to put their name on!<P>I will not be spending extra $$ on KYB if it is sold as a Gabriel for less $$!<P>So if you are buying a KYB strut are you getting your money's worth?<P>Paul<P>||||reg||5
